2. Background and Theoretical Foundations

This section briefly reviews foundational concepts, including parameter and structural plasticity, while a detailed comparison with prior art is deferred to the next section. The core principles of the stability-plasticity dilemma (Grossberg, 1987) and metaplasticity (Abraham & Bear, 1996) are introduced, framing them not as peripheral concepts but as central constraints on any self-modifying system.

