Appendix E: Formal Statements of Hypotheses and Statistical Protocols

This appendix provides the precise, pre-registered formulations of the three hypotheses and the statistical procedures that will be used to test them.

E.1 Hypothesis $\mathcal{H}_1$ (Continual Adaptation)

Formal Statement:
Let $\text{ACC}_C(T_1 \to T_2)$ denote the accuracy of System C on task $T_1$ after training on task $T_2$. The hypothesis is:
\mathbb{E}[\text{ACC}_C(T_1 \to T_2)] > \mathbb{E}[\text{ACC}_B(T_1 \to T_2)]


where $T_1$ and $T_2$ are tasks from a diverse set, and the expectation is over random seeds and task orderings.

Statistical Protocol:

· Effect Size: A meaningful effect is defined as a 5% improvement in retained accuracy.
· Sample Size: $N_{seeds} = 10$ random seeds per system.
· Test: Paired t-test comparing System C and System B on the retained accuracy metric.
· Correction: Bonferroni correction for multiple comparisons across different task sequences.

E.2 Hypothesis $\mathcal{H}_2$ (Structural Novelty)

Formal Statement:
The discovered topology $G_T$ contains motifs $M$ that are not present in $G_0$ and that have positive counterfactual utility:
\exists M \subset G_T : M \not\subset G_0 \text{ and } \Delta J_M > \theta_M

Statistical Protocol:

· Motif Identification: Use the FANMOD algorithm to identify recurrent motifs in $G_T$ and $G_0$.
· Counterfactual Utility: Perform ablation studies by removing the motif and measuring the change in performance.
· Significance Test: A one-sample t-test to determine if $\Delta J_M > 0$ with a significance level of $\alpha = 0.05$.

E.3 Hypothesis $\mathcal{H}_3$ (Emergent Capability)

Formal Statement:
For some capability $c$:
P_C(c) - P_A(c) > \theta_{\text{gap}}


and the robustness criteria for emergence (Section B.2) are satisfied.

Statistical Protocol:

· Robustness Analysis: Plot $P_C(c) - P_A(c)$ and the non-decomposability $N(c)$ as a function of the threshold parameters. Claims of emergence are only accepted if they hold over a continuous range of thresholds.
· Continuous Metrics: Report the continuous complexity gap $\Delta \hat{K}(c)$ and the performance gap $P_C(c) - P_A(c)$ as primary metrics, avoiding reliance on binary thresholding.

